  "readinessHowBody": "Everyone has different normal values, so GymBar compares your data with your own average over the last 60 days (14 days of data are enough to start). HRV is rated as a 7-day average because the daily value fluctuates a lot; normal is the average ± 0.75 standard deviations (based on HRV4Training and studies by Plews et al.). A resting heart rate 5+ beats above average is a warning; 3 days in a row can mean you are getting ill. Sleep: adults need at least 7 hours (AASM 2015); under 6 h counts as sleep loss, and after several short nights strength in compound lifts drops (Knowles et al. 2018). Heart rate zones use a max heart rate of 208 − 0.7 × age (Tanaka 2001), energy follows Keytel et al. (2005). This is not a medical assessment – if you don’t feel well, listen to your body.",
